1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
steel box beams carried the walkway load

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
hanger rods threaded through the channels

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
the nut seated against the washer flange

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
weld beads joined the channels toe to toe

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
the flange tapered toward the toe edge

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
rods held while the steel tore open

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
friction piles stopped short of bedrock

8
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
concrete footings settled into soft silt

9
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
the tower leaned further every year

10
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
soil tests showed deep soft clay

11
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
bedrock lay far below the piles

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
engineers drilled deeper test borings

13
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
investigators recovered the broken connections

14
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
the federal report listed failed welds

15
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
engineers examined every recovered beam

16
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,000
findings pointed to doubled connection loads

17
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,000
the inquiry heard sworn testimony

18
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
the final report named the fatal change

19
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
lawsuits followed the collapse for years

20
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:42,000
settlements reached millions of dollars

21
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
the state revoked engineering licenses

22
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,000
courts heard negligence claims daily

23
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:03,000
families sought damages and answers

24
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:10,000
regulators rewrote connection review rules
